  "question": {
    "text": "In Carius method of estimation of halogens, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>250</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mg</mi></math> of an organic compound gave <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>141</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>AgBr</mi></math>. What is the percentage of bromine in the compound (atomic mass of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ag</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>108</mn></math>&nbsp;and atomic number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Br</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn></math>)?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "EP7tg",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn></math>",
